commit 15d76fc0951603d1cc83080713e4753f303818b2
Author:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Thu Aug 20 12:52:17 2026 -0500
Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 20 12:52:17 2026 -0500

    fix(atoms,engine): a non-mapping payload is a missing-K non-member
    
    Fact permits any JSON payload and SqliteStore persists one, so a scalar or
    list payload reaches every reader of a ByKey(payload_field) projection. Both
    the mapping-shaped family rule (atoms.resolve_key_field) and the row-shaped
    combined-read accessor (engine._row_field) called .get() on it and raised
    AttributeError, taking the whole read down.
    
    A payload that is not a mapping has no field K in exactly the sense an absent
    field does, so it resolves to None — the missing-K non-member rule, exclusion
    by declaration. The payload half of the rule is split out as
    atoms.resolve_payload_key so the row-shaped accessor resolves through the SAME
    definition rather than repeating .get(); one definition, not two spellings
    that can disagree.
    
    Envelope keys (ts/id) are unaffected: they are always present regardless of
    payload shape. StoreReader.ordered and the conformance lens generator inherit
    the fix through resolve_key_field.
    
    Refs: C-SOL-01 (sol r1, major)
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JpCUT3bF3dukDk5xjDejRM

