commit bd7c6abcda60bfb75c28db9c7c1b6d52024f54c4
Author:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Thu Aug 20 12:54:08 2026 -0500
Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 20 12:54:08 2026 -0500

    fix(engine): the aggregate Arrival refusal is declaration-shaped
    
    _combined_read returned empty state before resolving the declared ordering,
    so an aggregate whose members were all currently unresolvable ACCEPTED
    Arrival() and began refusing it only once enough members came back. That makes
    the mandatory refusal a function of current file availability rather than of
    the declaration.
    
    Resolve the ordering before the empty-members return. An aggregate with zero
    resolvable members still has no cross-store arrival axis, so it refuses
    exactly as a populated one does; the default (and any valid declared ordering)
    still returns empty state unchanged.
    
    sdk read_facts was audited and already keys on DECLARATION SHAPE rather than
    member count, so it needed no change — pinned so a later refactor cannot
    reintroduce the hole there. resolve_entity takes no declared ordering and has
    no refusal to skip.
    
    Refs: C-SOL-02 (sol r1, major)
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JpCUT3bF3dukDk5xjDejRM

