    spec(conformance): lens vector for non-mapping payload non-membership
    
    A third posture in the missing-K family, alongside the absent field and the
    explicit null: a payload that is not a mapping at all. Fact permits any JSON
    payload, and this implementation raised AttributeError on one (C-SOL-01), so
    it is exactly the posture a reimplementation would plausibly get wrong — and
    the vectors are where a cross-implementation rule belongs.
    
    The six pre-existing normative files regenerate byte-identically (sha256
    verified before/after); only the new file is added. The vector is
    mutation-proof: dropping the isinstance guard in atoms.resolve_payload_key
    fails it.
    
    Refs: C-SOL-01 (sol r1, major)
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JpCUT3bF3dukDk5xjDejRM

