## New findings

### C-SOL-05 — minor — [ordering.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/atoms/src/atoms/ordering.py:232)

**Claim:** NaN validation occurs during the single-pass type scan, so a mixed-type projection’s refusal category depends on which value appears first. This contradicts the remediation claim that the type check wins over NaN.

```text
NaN mixed-type permutations:
  ('n', 'i') => OrderingError: NaN key value under declared key 'k': nan
  ('i', 'n') => OrderingError: mixed key types under declared key 'k':
                int and float (offending value nan)
```

Both inputs contain precisely the same key values. A complete type-identity pass must precede NaN validation if mixed-type refusal is intended to win consistently.

### C-SOL-06 — nit — [test_ordering.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/atoms/tests/test_ordering.py:145)

**Claim:** The docstring ratchet searches individual lines for contiguous phrases, making a newline a complete evasion. It also hardcodes four inspected objects rather than walking all module docstrings.

